- Something happened

00:03:46.783 --> 00:03:47.616
before the encore.

00:03:47.616 --> 00:03:49.990
My personal encore of a meal happened.

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:51.170
- Wow, on stage?

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:52.590
- Uh, no, no, no.

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:55.380
I ran backstage and was
very like pro about it

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.350
and then was not.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:58.730
But it's interesting because
if you think about it

00:03:58.730 --> 00:03:59.910
the stage is built in an arena.

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:02.250
There's thousands of people cheering me on

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.153
while this is all happening.

00:04:04.153 --> 00:04:04.986
- Yeah, yeah.

00:04:04.986 --> 00:04:07.780
- While I'm having my own
personal bridesmaids moment.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.250
- What was the song
right before that moment?

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.940
Cause obviously you can
feel this coming on.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:13.790
This is gonna go pear
shaped here real quick.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:14.790
- Oh, no. Here's the best part.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:15.623
I don't even remember.

00:04:15.623 --> 00:04:17.250
It was probably like "Since
You've Been Gone" or whatever.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.083
Something like that, it
was probably like that,

00:04:18.083 --> 00:04:20.940
but it was like right when
I had to come back on.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:23.760
I was about to go on stage and
sing "The Greatest Showman",

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:25.390
We did a re-imagined thing
and it was "Never Enough."

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:28.270
And it's like very intense
and the sun is passed away

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:29.500
and I'm trying to get in the mood

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:31.740
while secretly I'm like
"Don't happen again, please."

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:32.590
- Right, yeah.

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:34.136
- Yeah. Has that ever happened to you?

00:04:34.136 --> 00:04:36.279
- Not to that degree.
- Oh, stop.

00:04:36.279 --> 00:04:39.590
You let me go through all
that and you gave me nothing!

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.262
- No, I haven't had
anything like that happen.

00:04:42.262 --> 00:04:43.095
- No?

00:04:43.095 --> 00:04:44.010
- No. I split my pants on stage.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.330
- Oh, I've done that too.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:46.620
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:48.040
- And that's when you wish the guitar

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:49.533
was more so in the back butt.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:51.870
- Mine was at a video shoot.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:52.830
I split my pants

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:54.410
at "Since You've Been
Gone" video, actually.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:56.020
- Wow. You gotta stop singing that song.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:57.970
- I know. This song is not good for me.

00:04:59.295 --> 00:05:00.806
- Well, do you forget lyrics or anything?

00:05:00.806 --> 00:05:02.640
Do you ever forget where
you're at in the show?

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:04.140
- I'm pretty good with lyrics.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:07.070
One time I forgot the words to the song

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:09.540
and I'm singing along and I'm just singing

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:12.460
and in my head I'm thinking,
"What's the next verse?"

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:13.810
I'm like, "Oh, I don't
know it. I don't know it."

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:15.927
And it came. And I was like
(mumbles indistinctively),

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:21.458
and I'm wriggling this mic.

00:05:21.458 --> 00:05:23.850
(mic sounds)

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:26.810
- Wait, did you pretend that
there was a malfunction?

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:29.450
- Yeah.
- You are so smart.

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:33.088
(audience applause)

00:05:33.088 --> 00:05:35.127
I'm stealing this as well.

00:05:35.127 --> 00:05:36.550
- There's a bit more to the story.

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:38.850
So, I apparently did it so well

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.520
that one of the road crew ran out

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.170
and replaced the mic immediately.

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:45.840
But by then I knew what the lyrics were

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:46.740
so it was all good.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.090
- Oh, my God.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:49.225
Oh man, I forget lyrics

00:05:49.225 --> 00:05:50.058
all the time.
- Because this thing

00:05:50.058 --> 00:05:51.633
to the audience is a giveaway, right?

00:05:51.633 --> 00:05:52.670
- I do it, though.

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:54.543
I'm like "Jesus, help me"

00:05:56.558 --> 00:05:57.391
And then I own it.

00:05:57.391 --> 00:05:59.870
I'm like, I wrote it, I don't remember it.

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:00.780
I don't know what's happening.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.480
I'm like making a list of
things to do in my head.

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:03.510
I don't know what's happening.

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:05.010
You've made music with many people

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:08.455
from Taylor Swift to Pink, who I love.

00:06:08.455 --> 00:06:10.300
- Yeah, I love her.
- Oh, my God. I love it.

